This feature allows MME to send different network names (PLMN name/SPN)
to UEs based on their Tracking Area Code (TAC), enabling tenant-specific
branding in multi-tenant deployments.

Key changes:
- Extended tenant_control configuration to support network_name per TAC
- Added mme_get_network_name_for_tac() with fallback to global config
- Modified emm_handle_attach_complete() to use TAC-specific network name
- Network names encoded in UCS-2 format (similar to global config)
- Thread-safe access using existing tenant_control_mutex

Configuration example:
  tenant_control:
    - tenant_id: "tenant1"
      tac: 1
      network_name:
        full: "Operator A"
        short: "Op-A"

Behavior:
- Uses TAC-specific name if configured
- Falls back to global mme.network_name if not configured
- Backward compatible with existing configurations

Also fixed update_nf_binary.sh to use correct build path.

